    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>kafedra-flow-intake: define desktop current/archive navigation states</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Switching the register is one action and never archives or restores a plan.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The existing status query remains authoritative and search/ordinary filters survive.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>An invalid selected plan cannot remain as stale detail.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Below 721 pixels the original select is restored without a new state machine.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/lifecycle.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>kafedra-design: specify persistent desktop segmented hierarchy and exact fallback</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001/></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The segment is permanently visible only at desktop widths and visually distinct from ordinary filters.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Selection is expressed by text, shape and accessibility state, not color alone.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Each segment has a 44 pixel target and visible focus.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The source select recovers its original hidden, aria-hidden and tabindex attributes below the breakpoint.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>kafedra-motion: keep lifecycle switching synchronous and no-motion</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-002/></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>No request, focus change, empty state or fallback waits for an animation event.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The segment uses no decorative movement and remains equivalent with reduced motion.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>kafedra-feature: implement a desktop adapter over the existing select authority</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-003/></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The adapter emits the existing select input/change events and contains no API or persistence layer.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>DOM rerenders and width transitions do not duplicate controls or listeners.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Desktop keyboard and empty-state behavior is deterministic.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Narrow width removes the adapter and restores the original select exactly.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/plans-lifecycle-desktop.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-004>
      <T-005>
        <Title>kafedra-design-audit and kafedra-tests: verify desktop behavior and narrow fallback</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-004/></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Independent audit has no blocker for hierarchy, focus, target size, text states or no-motion behavior.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Desktop Playwright covers status requests, search retention, stale detail, repeated action and 1440 to 720 to 1440 restoration.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Full project CI remains green and no mobile-specific product behavior is added.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm test</Command><Command>npx playwright test tests/browser/plans-lifecycle-desktop.spec.mjs --project=desktop</Command></Verification>
      </T-005>
      <T-006>
        <Title>kafedra-release: exact-head merge, post-merge and terminal archive</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-005/></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Every required check succeeds on one unchanged PR head.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Squash merge is followed by successful post-merge CI.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>A separate archive-only PR moves the complete bundle to terminal applied state before issue closure.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run check</Command><Command>npm run docs:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-006>
